---
import { identity } from "../data/ascii";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import TerminalLayout from "../layouts/TerminalLayout.astro";
---

<TerminalLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Benjamin Anderson, an electronics engineer working across hardware, firmware and product design."
  path="~/about"
  command="whoami"
>
  <div class="term-neofetch">
    <pre class="term-ascii" aria-hidden="true">{identity}</pre>

    <dl class="term-facts">
      <dt>user</dt>
      <dd>{site.name}</dd>

      <dt>role</dt>
      <dd>Electronics engineer</dd>

      <dt>focus</dt>
      <dd>Hardware design, embedded systems and PCB development</dd>

      <dt>tools</dt>
      <dd>KiCad, FreeCAD, Blender, OpenSCAD, C, C++, Python</dd>

      <dt>education</dt>
      <dd>Electronic engineering graduate</dd>

      <dt>currently</dt>
      <dd>Rebuilding engiebenji.com</dd>

      <dt>links</dt>
      <dd>
        <a href={site.github} rel="me">
          GitHub
        </a>
        <a href={site.linkedin} rel="me">
          LinkedIn
        </a>
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Email</a>
        <a href={site.cv}>CV</a>
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <div class="term-prose">
    <p>
      I enjoy the process of moulding the ideas in my head into something
      tangible, then fine tuning it until it is exactly what I envisioned.
      Whether it is the PCBs controlling a new device, the renders for a project
      thumbnail, or the code that makes it work, I care about the details.
    </p>
    <p>
      My work sits between electronics and product design: schematic capture and
      PCB layout, firmware, mechanical design, and the small tools that make the
      next build easier. I am particularly interested in projects that reward
      careful iteration, from custom input devices to compact display hardware.
    </p>
  </div>
</TerminalLayout>
